  "help_content": "Calculations & Algorithm:\nCalculations in Buddhist Sun are powered by the National Renewable Energy Laboratory's Solar Position Algorithm (NREL SPA). Unlike older algorithms (such as Meeus) which had up to a 1-minute margin of error, NREL SPA is the international gold standard and is accurate to within a few seconds for solar noon, sunrise, and twilights.\n\nImportant Vinaya Precaution:\nWhile the astronomical calculation is accurate within a few seconds, monks and 8/10-precept practitioners should be sure not to swallow any food and rinse the mouth one minute to 30 seconds before the time expires so that no food particles remain in the mouth or throat when solar noon arrives.\n\nApplication Features:\n• Solar Noon & Dawn: High-precision solar noon and customizable dawn formulas (Pa-Auk -40m, Na-Uyana -30m, astronomical twilights, and custom angles).\n• Hands-Free Voice Countdown: Spoken voice notifications (TTS) with screen-off background support warning at critical intervals down to zero.\n• Vinaya Compass: 3D Great-Circle Earth globe, 2D map, and Buddhist rotating dial aligned toward Bodh Gaya and other holy pilgrimage destinations.\n• Moon Phase & Uposatha Calendar: Daily lunar phase percentage and traditional Uposatha / Poya days across Thai, Myanmar, and Sri Lanka traditions.\n• Sun & Shadow (Vinaya Ratio): Real-time stick shadow angle and finger-breadth (angula) measurement for physical noon verification.\n• Buddhavassa (BE Calendar): Buddhist Era year calculations, vassa counts, and Pakkha calendar days.\n• Meditation Timer: Mindful timer with singing bowl chimes, interval bells, and warm-up periods.\n• Maraṇassati (Death Contemplation): Mindfulness of mortality with life expectancy analytics and contemplation alerts.\n• GPS & 40,000+ City Database: High-accuracy GPS detection or offline city lookup worldwide.\n• Safety Offsets: Configurable safety buffer (1–10 minutes) subtracting from noon or adding to dawn for peace of mind.\n\nPrivacy:\nBuddhist Sun does not collect personal information.\nFull statement: https://americanmonk.org/privacy-policy-for-buddhist-sun-app/",
  "about_content": "Buddhist Sun is a small app for Buddhist monks and nuns to display the Solar Noon time specific to Buddhist monastic needs. Because I usually eat with my hands, I needed to have a \"hands free\" way to know when the Noon was approaching. The timer with voice notifications turned on helps me know the time left for eating.  I enjoy using the app, and I hope that you do too.\n\nWhy is this important?\nThose who follow Buddhist monastic rules are not allowed to eat after Noon.  The rule is according to the sun at its zenith in the sky rather than a clock. They did not have clocks in the Buddha's time.  Others who follow 8 or 10 precepts may find this app useful too.\n\nI recommend https://www.kso.ac.at/beobachtungen/ephemeris_en.php  to verify this app's accuracy.  The Buddhist Era page was made by Bhante Amarawali of Yogashrama. The contact email address is bhamarawali@gmail.com.  This application is meant for \"present moment/location\" use.  \n\nMay this help you to reach Nibbāna quickly and safely!",
  "gps_permission_content": "Permission will be requested for GPS use. This allows for Buddhist Sun to know the GPS Location Data to calculate the sun's position. GPS is only collected once for each time the GPS button is pressed.  Data is not sent outside this app.",
  "background_permission_content": "Permission will be requested for background use.  This permission is needed to enable speech notifications to run properly even when the screen is off.  Buddhist Sun will turn off this Background process when the switch is turned off or the app is closed.  Permission will be requested only one time if accepted.",
  "dstSavingsNotice": "Warning, this app does not calculate for Daylight Savings Time (DST).  Please be aware of the changes.  When DST happens you need to reset the GPS or the offset found in the Settings Tab.",
