  "vitDTodayInfoTitle": "About today's estimate",
  "vitDTodayInfo": "Today's total adds up the vitamin D estimated from all of today's sessions, including one that is running. It resets at midnight.\n\nThe percentage compares it with your daily target of {iu} IU. Reaching 100% is enough for the day; more sun adds little and raises the burn dose.\n\nThese are rough estimates in the same units as supplements: about 1,000 IU from the sun has roughly the same effect on blood levels as a 1,000 IU tablet. Real amounts vary with haze, ozone, age and how much skin faces the sun.\n\nOfficial advice is 600 IU a day (800 IU over age 70). The automatic target here uses about 20 IU per kg of body weight; you can set your own in Sun Settings.\n\nVitamin D is stored in the body for weeks, so the weekly total matters more than any single day.",
